  "summary": "The Renton City Council on July 6 tabled a vote on un-pausing its ALPR/Flock camera program until all councilmembers complete an orientation with the Renton Police Department. The cameras have been paused since May 4 amid public concerns about surveillance, data access, immigration enforcement, and misuse.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "the Renton City Council voted to essentially table a vote on un-pausing the ALPR cameras in the city until all council members have completed an orientation and training on the technology provided by the Renton Police Department",
      "paragraph_idx": 6
    },
    {
      "quote": "The council paused the police's use of the cameras on May 4 for the council members to \"get more information to address the concerns of the public\" on the technology.",
      "paragraph_idx": 7
    },
    {
      "quote": "the cameras captured 5,271,962 images, but officers only viewed 461 in 390 searches",
      "paragraph_idx": 12
    }
  ],
